      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of insignificance, where the sheer scale of the world makes your individual existence feel meaningless, is a very common, yet deeply painful, human experience. It's not illogical; it's a response to feeling overwhelmed by the vastness of life and the weight of your own smallness. If this sense of meaninglessness is persistent, talking to a therapist can help you explore these deep philosophical feelings and find more personal anchors. Please remember that even if you feel like a drop in the ocean, your experience matters.",
      "source": "target",
